# {{project_name}}

A MuduDB application written in AssemblyScript, packaged as
`{{module_name}}.mpk`. Scaffolded with `mpm-crate` — edit this project
freely; it is a starting point, not a generated artifact.

It defines three tables (`items`, `item_info`, `item_info_labels`, see
`sql/ddl.sql`) and two Mudu Procedures (see `assembly/procedures.ts`):
`create_item` (scalar arguments) and `update_item_info`, which demonstrates
a **user-defined record type** — the `item-info` record declared in
`wit/types.wit` — as a procedure parameter and return type.

## Prerequisites

On PATH:

- `node` and `npm`
- `python3` (runs the wasm export patch script)
- `cargo-make` (`cargo install cargo-make`)
- `wasm-tools` (`cargo install wasm-tools`)
- `mgen`, `mtp`, `mpm-build` — the MuduDB toolchain
- `mpm-install`, `mudud`, `mcli` — to install and invoke the package

The binding comes from the `@mududb/mududb` npm package (see
`package.json`). The record bridge (`recordFieldValues` /
`recordFromFieldValues`, used by the mtp-generated adapter for
`update_item_info`) requires a binding version that carries
`assembly/record.ts`; when the project is scaffolded from a mududb
repository checkout (`mpm-crate --sdk-path`), the `file:` dependency
points at that checkout's binding directly.

## Layout

- `sql/ddl.sql` — database schema; `sql/init.sql` — seed data.
- `assembly/procedures.ts` — hand-written procedures (`/**mudu-proc*/`
  marker; first parameter `id: Oid` is the bound session). Imports the SDK
  from the `@mududb/mududb` npm package (see `package.json`) and the
  project record type from `../gentypes/types`.
- `wit/types.wit` — the project's message types (the `item-info` record),
  consumed two ways: `mgen message` turns it into the AssemblyScript
  classes/codecs under `gentypes/`, and `mtp --type-wit` registers the
  names so procedure signatures may use them. The `package` clause is
  required: one WIT directory is one package.
- `gentypes/` — **generated by mgen** (`cargo make gentypes`): the
  `ItemInfo` class plus its `ItemInfoCodec` codec (`types.ts`), and the
  `mpack.ts` re-export shim the generated file imports (staged from
  `build-cfg/gentypes-mpack.ts` by the `gentypes-shim` task). Never edit
  by hand.
- `assembly/items.ts` — the `items` entity record, its SQL statements and
  row codecs, **generated by `mgen entity`** from `sql/ddl.sql` on every
  build (one `<table>.ts` per table; do not edit by hand).
- `generated/` — the `mtp` byte-pipe adapter and world WIT (build artifact).
- `wit/deps/mududb-api/api.wit` — copy of the host syscall interface.
- `scripts/patch-component-exports.py` — renames the `mp2_*` wasm exports to
  the kebab-case component names `wasm-tools component new` looks up.
- `package/package.cfg.json` — package metadata; `package/package.desc.json`
  is regenerated by the build.

## Build

```bash
cargo make package
```

This runs `mgen entity` → `mgen message` (gentypes) → `npm install` → `mtp`
→ `mgen check-sql` → `asc` → patch script → `wasm-tools component
embed/new` → `mpm-build create`, producing
`target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{module_name}}.mpk`.

## Install and invoke

Start `mudud`, then:

```bash
mpm-install target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{module_name}}.mpk

mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc create_item \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "name": "pear"}'
```

## Records on the wire

A record argument travels as the positional `uni-data-value` record case
(field order = WIT declaration order, names dropped by the host); the guest
side never touches that envelope by hand — the mtp-generated adapter decodes
it through the binding record bridge (`recordFieldValues`) composed with the
mgen-generated `ItemInfoCodec`, and encodes a record result symmetrically
(`recordFromFieldValues` + `encodeProcedureOkUni`). Rules of the JSON/desc
surface:

- **JSON keys = WIT field names, verbatim** (`in-stock`, not `inStock`).
- **Booleans cross as 0/1** — the host has no boolean data-type family, so
  a WIT `bool` field is described as `I32` and takes JSON `0`/`1`.
- **u32/u16/u8 fields cross as i32**; missing JSON fields are an error,
  unknown keys are tolerated.

Invoke the record procedure with nested JSON:

```bash
mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc update_item_info \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "info": {"name": "pear", "price": 250, "in-stock": 1, "labels": ["fruit", "fresh"]}}'
```

`update_item_info` stores the record flattened into the `item_info` table
(the label list as `item_info_labels` side rows keyed by `(item_id, idx)`)
and returns the rebuilt record, updating the row by key and inserting it
on first write.

AssemblyScript v1 limits for user-defined types: `option<T>` parameters are
limited to `option<string>` and options of records; byte-array (`blob` /
`list<u8>`) record fields are supported in parameters only (record results
with byte-array fields are rejected at mtp time).

## Extending

- Add a procedure: export another `/**mudu-proc*/` function from
  `assembly/procedures.ts` and rebuild (the first parameter must be the
  `Oid` session; scalar parameters become procedure arguments).
- Add a record type: declare it in `wit/types.wit`, rebuild — `gentypes/`
  regenerates and the type becomes usable in procedure signatures.
- Add a table: extend `sql/ddl.sql`, rebuild, and import the regenerated
  entity (`import { <Record> } from "./<table>"`) for typed row codecs;
  `mgen check-sql` validates every SQL string against the schema on every
  build.
